Define what someone should be able to understand and do (@inquiry-learning-capability: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Diagnose-preparation-and-explain-a-dependency-before-naming-a-rule.lingua#r_00A948449B90BC0C5A2F092202") { r_0070DDB221FF1E371FDC6FCBDA
Teaching begins with someone who is to learn something for a purpose. A list of things mentioned in a lesson does not say what that person can do afterward. Start with an observable demand and the circumstances in which it matters. Our running example is a learner who must decide whether two paper jobs can pass through two workstations before a deadline, explain the decision and revise it when the calendar changes. The subject knowledge comes from [Count repeated visits before bounding useful output](../../engineering/core/Count-repeated-visits-before-bounding-useful-output.lingua#r_0042D69B36B9CD2481246608C5) and [Declare slot timing and reserve finite waiting spaces](../../engineering/core/Declare-slot-timing-and-reserve-finite-waiting-spaces.lingua#r_0002BF35AFDA5D67B939E8E57B); a teacher of this idea does not need to complete all of engineering first.

Use these distinct claims. Exposure means that material was available or presented. Assisted performance means that the learner completed a task with identified help. Independent performance means completion under declared conditions without that help. Retention asks whether relevant knowledge remains available after a stated interval. Transfer asks whether it can be used when important features of the task or setting change. Practical competence includes doing the relevant work under actual conditions, with appropriate judgment and evidence. These are operational distinctions for the investigation, not a universal numerical ladder of intelligence.

A learner can copy a valid schedule while the example is visible, yet fail to construct one from a blank calendar. Another can explain precedence aloud but misplace a token on a crowded board. Neither observation alone settles all six claims. Record the prompt, response, assistance, time, delay and materials. A drawing, spoken explanation or accessible representation can supply evidence when prose fluency is not the capability being assessed. If interpreting written instructions is itself the target, changing that demand changes what was assessed; describe the change.

For the present lesson the initial target is narrow: given at most two jobs, each requiring A followed by B, and a three-slot calendar, distinguish a capacity bound from a feasible schedule. The learner should construct a witness when possible, explain a temporal obstruction when impossible, and state the model assumptions. The later transfer target uses a changed dependency structure. A correct answer to the initial task is not a certificate for operating an industrial line.

**Work:** write a claim for one idea you need to learn and one method you need to hand over. Name the circumstances and evidence that would support each claim. Give two observations that might look successful yet fail to support it. Identify what could be demonstrated alone and what needs another person's observation, equipment or supervision. Reuse [Review reporting criticism and the limits of reproduced evidence](Review-reporting-criticism-and-the-limits-of-reproduced-evidence.lingua#r_00938E8A05E83C0B28227241FA) to keep proposed, performed and independently checked work separate.

**Continue:** [Diagnose preparation and explain a dependency before naming a rule](Diagnose-preparation-and-explain-a-dependency-before-naming-a-rule.lingua#r_00A948449B90BC0C5A2F092202).

